{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>This is the offering of Aaron.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory expounded that Moses was perplexed by four matters, and this is one of them. Their mnemonic is מקש\"ה. And the explanation of the verse in its secret sense: 'This is the offering of Aaron and his sons which they shall offer to YHWH' — for the attribute called 'this' they shall offer to YHWH by bringing a tenth of an ephah; and so the prophet mentioned for the future, at the initiation of the high priest's priesthood on the day of his inauguration, that he brings a tenth of an ephah, as it says (Ezekiel 44:27): ״וביום באו אל הקדש אל החצר הפנימית לשרת בקדש יקריב חטאתו״, and they said in the chapter אלו מגלחים: 'his sin-offering' — this is the tenth of an ephah, which is from the language of purging and purification."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Mnemonic מקש״ה appears to be an acronym; left untranslated as in the original. The phrase 'the attribute called זה' is rendered literally; the kabbalistic allusion is left cryptic as required."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:22.262692417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}